{
  "info": {
    "name": "HF Medusa — Suggestive Selling Store (Day 3–4 · Sơn)",
    "description": "Store-facing Suggestive Selling APIs — Sơn's Day 3 (filtering/ranking + cart rules CR-01..CR-04) and Day 4 (cache-aside, dismissal store D6, cart.updated invalidation, analytics events).\n\nEndpoints:\n- GET  /store/products/:id/suggestions   (2.5.1 — product-level, SUGG-001/002, filters 2.3.x)\n- GET  /store/carts/:id/suggestions       (2.5.2 — cart-level CR-01..04, SUGG-004, 2.4.x)\n- POST /store/suggestion-events           (2.5.3 / 2.6.8–2.6.12 — analytics)\n\nStore routes require the header 'x-publishable-api-key'. 'x-session-id' scopes dismissal + analytics (D6/SEC-04). Customer is derived from the (optional) bearer auth context — never from the body.\n\nRUN ORDER: open the 'Setup' folder and run top-to-bottom (Login → Get publishable key → Create cart → Add items). That fills {{token}}, {{publishableKey}} and {{cartId}} so the cart-level requests have data. Then run the 2.5.x folders (or use the Collection Runner).\n\nNOTE on data: suggestions follow the degrade contract (BR-10) — an empty catalog/rule mismatch returns HTTP 200 with an empty list, NOT an error. Tests therefore assert the response SHAPE (array + count + threshold_info), not non-emptiness. To get non-empty product-level results the seeded suggestion_rule + suggestion_rule_source must point at products that exist in the current catalog (reseed with `pnpm backend:seed` if they diverge).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:9009",
      "description": "backend port (.env PORT=9009)"
    },
    { "key": "adminEmail", "value": "postman@test.com" },
    { "key": "adminPassword", "value": "Supersecret123" },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "description": "admin JWT — auto-filled by Setup › Login"
    },
    {
      "key": "publishableKey",
      "value": "pk_160f5ac26e56619f4b1913353ebac7932a8c390e6a6379879df59db4a8b34de7",
      "description": "x-publishable-api-key (Default Publishable API Key from seed). Re-fetch via Setup › Get publishable key if it rotates."
    },
    {
      "key": "sessionId",
      "value": "sess_postman_demo",
      "description": "x-session-id — scopes dismissal set + analytics (D6/SEC-04)"
    },
    {
      "key": "regionId",
      "value": "reg_01KX54P002XZTC793GRS1QMW53",
      "description": "Vietnam / VND (from seed) — used to create the cart"
    },
    {
      "key": "productId",
      "value": "prod_01KX5SXC11R4JQY12RFMQ5KDW2",
      "description": "source product for product-level suggestions (apacs-astrox-77 racket)"
    },
    {
      "key": "suggestedProductId",
      "value": "prod_01KX5SXCQEVHZREH6STB68PYB1",
      "description": "product referenced in analytics events (apacs-bg66-ultimax string)"
    },
    {
      "key": "racketVariantId",
      "value": "variant_01KX5SXC62MSSX0CSA0GEGAPG3",
      "description": "apacs-astrox-77 variant — added to cart to fire cart rules"
    },
    {
      "key": "gripVariantId",
      "value": "variant_01KX5SXCV8E96PKNDREBJTHQB8",
      "description": "apacs-pu-overgrip variant — second add (triggers cart.updated for the invalidation flow)"
    },
    {
      "key": "cartId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "auto-filled by Setup › Create cart"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Setup (run in order)",
      "description": "Prepares {{token}}, {{publishableKey}} and {{cartId}} (with line items) so the cart-level requests below have data to work with.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (admin emailpass)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.token) { pm.collectionVariables.set('token', json.token); }",
                  "pm.test('got token', () => pm.expect(json.token).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/user/emailpass",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "user", "emailpass"]
            },
            "description": "Only needed to (optionally) re-fetch the publishable key below. Store suggestion/event calls are public — they use {{publishableKey}} directly."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get publishable key (admin, optional)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "const keys = j.api_keys || [];",
                  "if (keys[0] && keys[0].token) { pm.collectionVariables.set('publishableKey', keys[0].token); }",
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('has a publishable key', () => pm.expect(keys.length).to.be.above(0));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/api-keys?type=publishable&limit=1",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "api-keys"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "type", "value": "publishable" },
                { "key": "limit", "value": "1" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Refreshes {{publishableKey}} from the admin API in case the seeded key rotated. Requires {{token}} (Login first)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create cart",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (j.cart && j.cart.id) { pm.collectionVariables.set('cartId', j.cart.id); }",
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('cart created', () => pm.expect(j.cart.id).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "x-publishable-api-key", "value": "{{publishableKey}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"region_id\": \"{{regionId}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/store/carts",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["store", "carts"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Add racket to cart (fires cart rules + cart.updated)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('cart has items', () => pm.expect(j.cart.items.length).to.be.above(0));",
                  "// Adding a line item emits cart.updated → the subscriber invalidates the cart suggestion cache (2.6.1/2.6.6)."
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "x-publishable-api-key", "value": "{{publishableKey}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"variant_id\": \"{{racketVariantId}}\",\n  \"quantity\": 1\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/store/carts/{{cartId}}/line-items",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["store", "carts", "{{cartId}}", "line-items"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2.5.1 · GET product suggestions",
      "description": "Product-level \"Complete Your Setup\" (SUGG-001/002). Public [C] + x-publishable-api-key. Day-3 filters (in-cart / out-of-stock / dismissed / recent-purchase — 2.3.1–2.3.4), ranking (2.3.5) and the ≤5 limit (2.3.6). Day-4: the raw enriched buffer is cached per product on the no-cart path; the dismissal set (x-session-id) is applied at runtime.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Product suggestions (basic)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 (never 5xx — BR-10)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('suggestions is an array', () => pm.expect(j.suggestions).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('count matches length', () => pm.expect(j.count).to.eql(j.suggestions.length));",
                  "pm.test('respects PRODUCT_LIMIT (<=5)', () => pm.expect(j.suggestions.length).to.be.at.most(5));",
                  "if (j.suggestions.length) {",
                  "  const s = j.suggestions[0];",
                  "  pm.test('item has contract fields', () => pm.expect(s).to.include.keys('product_id','name','price','tier','display_order'));",
                  "  pm.test('tier is manual|category', () => pm.expect(['manual','category']).to.include(s.tier));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "x-publishable-api-key", "value": "{{publishableKey}}" },
              { "key": "x-session-id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/store/products/{{productId}}/suggestions",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["store", "products", "{{productId}}", "suggestions"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "… with cart_id (in-cart filter 2.3.1)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('suggestions is an array', () => pm.expect(j.suggestions).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('none of the suggestions are already in the cart (2.3.1)', () => {",
                  "  // in-cart products are filtered out server-side; we just assert the shape holds",
                  "  pm.expect(j.count).to.eql(j.suggestions.length);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "x-publishable-api-key", "value": "{{publishableKey}}" },
              { "key": "x-session-id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/store/products/{{productId}}/suggestions?cart_id={{cartId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["store", "products", "{{productId}}", "suggestions"],
              "query": [{ "key": "cart_id", "value": "{{cartId}}" }]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "… with limit=3 (clamp 2.3.6)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('honours limit (<=3)', () => pm.expect(j.suggestions.length).to.be.at.most(3));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "x-publishable-api-key", "value": "{{publishableKey}}" },
              { "key": "x-session-id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/store/products/{{productId}}/suggestions?limit=3",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["store", "products", "{{productId}}", "suggestions"],
              "query": [{ "key": "limit", "value": "3" }]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "… unknown product → 200 empty (degrade BR-10)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 (never 5xx)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('empty suggestions', () => pm.expect(j.suggestions).to.eql([]));",
                  "pm.test('count 0', () => pm.expect(j.count).to.eql(0));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "x-publishable-api-key", "value": "{{publishableKey}}" },
              { "key": "x-session-id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/store/products/prod_does_not_exist/suggestions",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": [
                "store",
                "products",
                "prod_does_not_exist",
                "suggestions"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2.5.2 · GET cart suggestions",
      "description": "Cart-level \"You Might Also Need\" (SUGG-004). Runs CR-01..CR-04 in priority order (2.4.7), ≤3 unique across rules (2.4.8), threshold_info only when CR-02 fires (2.4.10), hides the section when empty (2.4.9). Day-4: raw result cached under suggest:cart:v{version}:{cartId}; dismissal (x-session-id) applied at runtime.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Cart suggestions",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 (never 5xx — BR-10)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('suggestions is an array', () => pm.expect(j.suggestions).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('count matches length', () => pm.expect(j.count).to.eql(j.suggestions.length));",
                  "pm.test('respects CART_LIMIT (<=3)', () => pm.expect(j.suggestions.length).to.be.at.most(3));",
                  "pm.test('threshold_info is null or {target,current,remaining} (2.4.10)', () => {",
                  "  if (j.threshold_info !== null) pm.expect(j.threshold_info).to.have.all.keys('target','current','remaining');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('empty section → threshold_info null (2.4.9)', () => {",
                  "  if (j.suggestions.length === 0) pm.expect(j.threshold_info).to.eql(null);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('each item carries rule_code CR-0x', () => {",
                  "  j.suggestions.forEach((s) => pm.expect(['CR-01','CR-02','CR-03','CR-04']).to.include(s.rule_code));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "x-publishable-api-key", "value": "{{publishableKey}}" },
              { "key": "x-session-id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/store/carts/{{cartId}}/suggestions",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["store", "carts", "{{cartId}}", "suggestions"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "… with limit=2",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('honours limit (<=2)', () => pm.expect(j.suggestions.length).to.be.at.most(2));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "x-publishable-api-key", "value": "{{publishableKey}}" },
              { "key": "x-session-id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/store/carts/{{cartId}}/suggestions?limit=2",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["store", "carts", "{{cartId}}", "suggestions"],
              "query": [{ "key": "limit", "value": "2" }]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "… unknown/empty cart → 200 empty (2.4.9 / BR-10)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 (never 5xx)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('empty suggestions', () => pm.expect(j.suggestions).to.eql([]));",
                  "pm.test('count 0', () => pm.expect(j.count).to.eql(0));",
                  "pm.test('threshold_info null', () => pm.expect(j.threshold_info).to.eql(null));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "x-publishable-api-key", "value": "{{publishableKey}}" },
              { "key": "x-session-id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/store/carts/cart_does_not_exist/suggestions",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["store", "carts", "cart_does_not_exist", "suggestions"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2.5.3 · POST suggestion-events",
      "description": "Batch analytics (SUGG-006). Fire-and-forget → always 202 {accepted, rejected}. Actions impression|tap|add_to_cart|dismiss (2.6.8–2.6.11), full payload (2.6.12). SEC-04: customer_id is taken from the auth context only (never the body); session_id falls back to the x-session-id header. Malformed events are rejected individually; batches over 10 are truncated.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "impression (product_view) — 2.6.8",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('202 Accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('accepted 1, rejected 0', () => { pm.expect(j.accepted).to.eql(1); pm.expect(j.rejected).to.eql(0); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "x-publishable-api-key", "value": "{{publishableKey}}" },
              { "key": "x-session-id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"events\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"impression\",\n      \"source_context\": \"product_view\",\n      \"source_product_id\": \"{{productId}}\",\n      \"suggested_product_id\": \"{{suggestedProductId}}\",\n      \"tier\": \"manual\",\n      \"slot\": 1\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/store/suggestion-events",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["store", "suggestion-events"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "tap — 2.6.9",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('202', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('accepted 1', () => pm.expect(j.accepted).to.eql(1));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "x-publishable-api-key", "value": "{{publishableKey}}" },
